    "title": "",
    "legend": "Mesenchymal chondrosarcoma is a biphasic sarcoma composed of primitive round to ovoid cells admixed with a well-differentiated cartilaginous component with central coarse calcifications. Note the hemangiopericytoma-like vascular pattern within the primitive component.",
    "source": "John M. Gross",
    "copyright": "",
