    "fileId": 54903,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Mesenchymal chondrosarcoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Mesenchymal chondrosarcoma is a biphasic sarcoma consisting of a primitive round / ovoid cells admixed with a second population of well-differentiated hyaline cartilage. Occasionally, through endochondral ossification of the cartilage, lamellar and/or woven bone will be form such as seen here in this extraskeletal (soft tissue) mesenchymal chondrosarcoma. ",
    "source": "John M. Gross",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
